// A label the language does not offer, named as an effect. Two answers, in this order:
// `eyg check` refuses the text before anything runs (`missing row 'Bash'`), and `eyg run` of
// the same text stops with `unhandled effect Bash` because no host has that label - the same
// answer inside a guarded call. Naming an effect is not the same as giving one a host.
// Run: eyg check test/fixtures/invented-effect.eyg
// Run: eyg run test/fixtures/invented-effect.eyg
// Run: node bin/agent/refusal-probe.mjs --program test/fixtures/invented-effect.eyg
perform Bash({ command: "id" })
